A polychrome sprite samples only inside its own atlas tile.

Atlas tiles pack edge to edge with no gutter and the sprite sampler is
bilinear. Once a sprite rotates or scales, the fragments along its edge
land within half a texel of the tile border and filter in whatever the
atlas packed next to it. A spinning disc in the cover panel showed this
as faint straight seams along its rotated bounding square, present or not
depending on the neighboring tile (#134). The fragment shader now clamps
the coordinate to the tile's outermost texel centers, on all three
backends.

Diffed against the tree with every earlier patch applied.

--- a/src/platform/blade/shaders.wgsl
+++ b/src/platform/blade/shaders.wgsl
@@ -1256,13 +1256,19 @@
 
 @fragment
 fn fs_poly_sprite(input: PolySpriteVarying) -> @location(0) vec4<f32> {
-    let sample = textureSample(t_sprite, s_sprite, input.tile_position);
+    let sprite = b_poly_sprites[input.sprite_id];
+    // rox patch: atlas tiles pack with no gutter, so a rotated or scaled
+    // sprite's edge fragments would filter in the neighboring tile's texels
+    // and draw a faint seam. Hold the sample to this tile's texel centers.
+    let atlas_size = vec2<f32>(textureDimensions(t_sprite, 0));
+    let tile_min = (vec2<f32>(sprite.tile.bounds.origin) + 0.5) / atlas_size;
+    let tile_max = (vec2<f32>(sprite.tile.bounds.origin + sprite.tile.bounds.size) - 0.5) / atlas_size;
+    let sample = textureSample(t_sprite, s_sprite, clamp(input.tile_position, tile_min, tile_max));
     // Alpha clip after using the derivatives.
     if (any(input.clip_distances < vec4<f32>(0.0))) {
         return vec4<f32>(0.0);
     }
 
-    let sprite = b_poly_sprites[input.sprite_id];
     let distance = quad_sdf(input.local_position, sprite.bounds, sprite.corner_radii);
 
     var color = sample;
